MID_EV13_005_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_005_m01_001: I see that you've received Mahadu's blessing.
MID_EV13_005_m01_002: That power will consume you, as it did him.\nWas this really the best course to take?
MID_EV13_005_m01_003: I would ask you a favor concerning this.
MID_EV13_005_m01_004: According to you, the arm ate away at\nMahadu's mind.
MID_EV13_005_m01_005: You must mention this—and the 10-year limit on\nmy life—to no one else.
MID_EV13_005_m01_006: You would bear a burden this heavy alone?
MID_EV13_005_m01_007: Not for nothing, I assure you.
MID_EV13_005_m01_008: This arm has granted me 10 years. I intend to\nuse them well.
MID_EV13_005_m01_009: What the million citizens of Saramis have longed\nfor, I will give to them.
MID_EV13_005_m01_010: I can tell you're resolved to do this.
MID_EV13_005_m01_011: If I can't dissuade you, I can at least give you\nthis warding chain.
MID_EV13_005_m01_012: <NCA>Inspect the chain.
MID_EV13_005_m01_013: What is this? It looks like jewelry of some kind.
MID_EV13_005_m01_014: Something like that. Your ancestors created it.\nI recommend wearing it on your right arm.
MID_EV13_005_m01_015: It will afford a measure of protection against the\nspirit's curse.
MID_EV13_005_m01_036: 
MID_EV13_005_m01_016: <NCA>Thank her.
MID_EV13_005_m01_017: <NCB>Play it off.
MID_EV13_005_m01_018: <ACA>My ancestors watch over me still... This is a\nthoughtful gift indeed.
MID_EV13_005_m01_019: <ACB>I doubt that will be necessary, but I appreciate your\nconsideration. For you, I will wear it.
MID_EV13_005_m01_020: But I warn you, Theodora. The warding chain will\nabsorb the arm's malice only up to a point.
MID_EV13_005_m01_021: If you see it begin to crack, it is straining against\nits limits. That may mean the end of you.
MID_EV13_005_m01_022: Pardon the interruption, Your Highness. We received\nan urgent report from Megaira.
MID_EV13_005_m01_023: No need for apologies. Our conversation was over.
MID_EV13_005_m01_024: From what we heard, Prince Dyan is pressing\nChancellor Kumos to begin his coronation.
MID_EV13_005_m01_025: What's the point in pressuring Kumos? Not like\nhe can hand Dyan the crown.
MID_EV13_005_m01_026: Besides, Kumos is too prim for that. The harder you\npush him, the firmer he stands.
MID_EV13_005_m01_027: We also learned that Prince Dyan is summoning\ncommanders to Megaira on pretext of an emergency.
MID_EV13_005_m01_028: No doubt he plans to force Kumos's hand through\na vote of the council of chieftains.
MID_EV13_005_m01_029: Time is of the essence, Your Highness!
MID_EV13_005_m01_030: We must show the people that you are as fit to rule\nas ever.
MID_EV13_005_m01_031: Wise counsel indeed.
MID_EV13_005_m01_032: We will return to Megaira without delay and put\nan end to Dyan's scheme!
MID_EV13_005_m01_033: Tobias! Bonaventure! Let us fly! And I'll hear not one\nword of complaint about our pace.
MID_EV13_005_m01_035: Right!
MID_EV13_006_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_006_m01_001: A strange place for such thick fog to set in...
MID_EV13_006_m01_002: Bonaventure! Tobias! Where are you?!
MID_EV13_006_m01_003: What's this? Who are you?
MID_EV13_006_m01_004: <NCA>Examine {AvatarGender=his|her} outfit.
MID_EV13_006_m01_005: <NCB>Examine {AvatarGender=his|her} feet.
MID_EV13_006_m01_006: <ACA>Your attire is strange. I know of no one among the\nforest clans who dresses this way.
MID_EV13_006_m01_007: <ACB>No shadow... Are you a spirit of this land?
MID_EV13_006_m01_008: We meet at last. I am here to provide guidance.
MID_EV13_006_m01_009: You are Theodora, the Breaker of Armies, one of\nthe Flame Lords of Dagda, are you not?
MID_EV13_006_m01_010: I am she, though I have never been known by those\ntitles. I notice you speak as humans do.
MID_EV13_006_m01_011: Then mark me when I inform you that you are in\nthe presence of royalty.
MID_EV13_006_m01_012: If you desire an audience, then observe common\ncourtesy and show the face beneath that hood.
MID_EV13_006_m01_013: Oh!
MID_EV13_006_m01_014: You remind me somewhat of Troy.
MID_EV13_006_m01_015: And your appearance... Might you be one of the\nPeople of the White Egg?
MID_EV13_006_m01_016: Listen well, little one.
MID_EV13_006_m01_017: A swirling vortex of causality yawns before you.
MID_EV13_006_m01_018: It will rage, and howl, and swallow you whole if\nit can.
MID_EV13_006_m01_019: Your trials will be many and arduous. Seek me out\nwhen you have overcome them.
MID_EV13_006_m01_020: Though as long as you carry this Divine Sand,\nI will never truly leave your side.
MID_EV13_006_m01_021: Good. Do not forget...
MID_EV13_006_m01_022: Wait! Damn it. Who the devil was that?
MID_EV13_006_m01_023: There you are, boss. What's with that look?\nDid something happen?
MID_EV13_006_m01_024: Please don't tell me you were harassed by ruffians—\nor worse!
MID_EV13_006_m01_025: No. Though...I'm not certain I could give a full\naccount of it. To be frank, it seemed a dream.
MID_EV13_006_m01_026: There was a person, clad all in white... Was it a\nspirit come to warn me?
MID_EV13_006_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}Hmph. Ever since returning to Megaira, I am plagued\nby strange occurrences.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_007_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_007_m01_001: To you nine mighty commanders who defend the\nlands composing Saramis...
MID_EV13_007_m01_002: I extend my gratitude to you fine chieftains for\nanswering my summons so promptly.
MID_EV13_007_m01_003: What are you playing at, Prince Dyan? Why have\nyou gathered the commanders here at Megaira?!
MID_EV13_007_m01_004: They're the cornerstones of our military might.\nHosting them all here will leave us defenseless!
MID_EV13_007_m01_005: Hold your tongue, Kumos. Their presence is\nrequired to hold a special council of chieftains.
MID_EV13_007_m01_006: You see, a council must be convened to ratify my\nearly claim to the throne.
MID_EV13_007_m01_007: Far worse for Saramis to remain leaderless than for\nour defenses to be temporarily thinned.
MID_EV13_007_m01_008: Everyone is saying so, at any rate. Though perhaps\nyou disagree, Chancellor?
MID_EV13_007_m01_009: Not just me. Our kingdom has always reserved the\nthrone for those who've come of age at 20 years.
MID_EV13_007_m01_010: You are still 18, Prince Dyan. This council shows\na flagrant disregard for tradition.
MID_EV13_007_m01_011: In the absence of a king, the council of chieftains\ncarries more weight than the chancellor alone.
MID_EV13_007_m01_012: So let us speak no more of tradition. All in support\nof my reign, raise your swords.
MID_EV13_007_m01_013: I see you've been busy politicking. However...
MID_EV13_007_m01_014: Your faction is still in the minority. So consider\nthis motion rejected.
MID_EV13_007_m01_015: Hrm...
MID_EV13_007_m01_016: What are you doing?!
MID_EV13_007_m01_017: Hyahaha! That's five in favor. And my vote as an\neligible candidate for the throne makes six.
MID_EV13_007_m01_018: Even assuming you vote nay, Chancellor, I count only\nfive in your corner. The motion carries!
MID_EV13_007_m01_019: You were busier even than I knew. I can see when\nI'm outmaneuvered, Prince Dyan.
MID_EV13_007_m01_020: But you, Commander Huver... I thought better of you\nthan to side with such a man as this.
MID_EV13_007_m01_021: Why would you go along with this farce, knowing\nthe wishes of the late King Sergio?!
MID_EV13_007_m01_043: Is that the Monarch's Axe? It's huge.
MID_EV13_007_m01_044: How's Prince Dyan planning to lift it with those\nnoodly arms?
MID_EV13_007_m01_045: *sigh*
MID_EV13_007_m01_046: {SetColor=Gray}Hyehehe. This should pose no difficulty, given\nthe trick I have in store.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_007_m01_047: {SetColor=Gray}One sip of this flamma and I'll have the strength to\ndo whatever they ask of me.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_007_m01_048: {SetColor=Gray}I certainly paid that northern merchant enough for\nthe privilege...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_007_m01_049: {SetColor=Gray}But any price would be worth it to lift this oversized\naxe as if it were a feather.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_007_m01_022: Hold! I cannot let you thr— Waaah!
MID_EV13_007_m01_023: I have come to object in the strongest possible terms.
MID_EV13_007_m01_024: My dear sister... What a surprise it is to see you\nhere alive.
MID_EV13_007_m01_025: Answer me this, Prince Dyan. What is a kingdom?
MID_EV13_007_m01_026: Every schoolchild knows that. A kingdom is a parcel\nof land ruled over by a powerful king!
MID_EV13_007_m01_027: You answered as expected, Prince Dyan: incorrectly.
MID_EV13_007_m01_028: A kingdom is its people. It is formed when those\npeople gather in unity under a king.
MID_EV13_007_m01_029: People are measured by the caliber of their hearts.\nAnd a kingdom without a heart is doomed to fall.
MID_EV13_007_m01_030: Forgive my impertinence, Prince, but you are\nill-suited to rallying the hearts of the people.
MID_EV13_007_m01_031: My late King Sergio knew this well. It is why he\nchose Princess Theodora as his successor!
MID_EV13_007_m01_032: What drivel. Without her arm, my sister could never\nhope to hoist this axe.
MID_EV13_007_m01_033: She has no standing to object. Guards! Take these\ninterlopers from my sight.
MID_EV13_007_m01_034: I will not be removed so easily, Dyan.
MID_EV13_007_m01_052: Hyah!
MID_EV13_007_m01_035: No... How have you regained your right arm?!\nIt was severed clean!
MID_EV13_007_m01_036: Princess Theodora? How can this be?!
MID_EV13_007_m01_038: Our great ancestor has granted me another chance.
MID_EV13_007_m01_039: Unfortunately for you, your flimsy scheme is about to\nbe trampled underfoot.
MID_EV13_007_m01_050: Rrah!
MID_EV13_007_m01_051: Uwah!
MID_EV13_007_m01_040: It is over, Dyan. I know it was your hand that steered\nthis recent turmoil.
MID_EV13_007_m01_041: Surrender yourself to be judged.
MID_EV13_007_m01_042: S-silence! Commanders! End this woman's life!
MID_EV13_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_008_m01_001: Submit, Dyan. Your sins have caught up with you.
MID_EV13_008_m01_002: Though you did not bloody your own hands, I charge\nyou with Father's death.
MID_EV13_008_m01_003: Come now, my dear sister. I'm within your power.\nI've learned my lesson, I swear it.
MID_EV13_008_m01_004: Don't you remember when we got along?!
MID_EV13_008_m01_005: How we would talk of our lofty plans for the future\nof Saramis?!
MID_EV13_008_m01_006: Those flower crowns I would craft for you!\nI always cared for you—can't you see that?
MID_EV13_008_m01_007: Mmm...
MID_EV13_008_m01_008: Your Highness...showing mercy to Prince Dyan now\nmay pose problems for you in the future.
MID_EV13_008_m01_009: <NCA>Give your verdict.
MID_EV13_008_m01_010: You shall live out the rest of your days under guard\nat Fort Cottus.
MID_EV13_008_m01_011: F...Fort Cottus?! No... Please! Not there!
MID_EV13_008_m01_012: Take him away. May I never see his face again.
MID_EV13_008_m01_013: Are you certain of this, Your Highness?
MID_EV13_008_m01_014: Some of the fault for his twisted nature may lie\nwith me.
MID_EV13_008_m01_015: Fear not. Cottus is an isolated island far out at sea.\nEscape is impossible—he may as well be dead.
MID_EV13_008_m01_016: I am more concerned with what was negotiated\nbetween Dyan and those who cast votes for him.
MID_EV13_008_m01_017: Perhaps they desired the assurance of status that\nDyan's coronation would offer.
MID_EV13_008_m01_018: You fought well, Princess.
MID_EV13_008_m01_019: Huver. My father spoke often of your\nexceptional loyalty.
MID_EV13_008_m01_020: I don't understand, Huver. You knew the late king\nwanted Princess Theodora to succeed him.
MID_EV13_008_m01_021: How could a man so loyal as you fail to honor\nhis wishes?
MID_EV13_008_m01_022: <NCA>Question Huver.
MID_EV13_008_m01_023: <NCB>Give your verdict.
MID_EV13_008_m01_024: <ACA>I would know what drove you to side with Dyan.
MID_EV13_008_m01_027: <ACA>I owed the house of Dyan's mother a debt\nof gratitude.
MID_EV13_008_m01_028: <ACA>I was obliged to extend that debt to Prince Dyan.
MID_EV13_008_m01_029: Haah...
MID_EV13_008_m01_030: You are relieved of duty as commander, Huver,\nand your family's lands are forfeit.
MID_EV13_008_m01_031: Your new position as staff officer in my retinue will\nbe hard work. I expect you to be prepared.
MID_EV13_008_m01_032: What?! But I am a traitor to your rule, Princess\nTheodora. Will that not set a bad precedent?
MID_EV13_008_m01_033: For your actions in siding with Dyan, you are\nbeing demoted. That is punishment enough.
MID_EV13_008_m01_034: I have need now of loyal retainers who are dutiful\nto a fault.
MID_EV13_008_m01_035: There will be a reckoning in the military as a result\nof today's events. I will require supporters.
MID_EV13_008_m01_036: If you feel this decision is unfair in your favor, then\nbalance the scales through loyal service.
MID_EV13_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_009_m01_001: I am honored to see you all here for my coronation.
MID_EV13_009_m01_002: Listen well, each of you, and bear witness to what\nI tell you here and now.
MID_EV13_009_m01_003: I, Theodora Sergio Savangren, will inherit the throne\nof the great King Sergio.
MID_EV13_009_m01_004: Let all gathered here know that I intend to serve you\nas the new queen of Saramis.
MID_EV13_009_m01_005: I vow to be a righteous leader.
MID_EV13_009_m01_006: My reign will see an end to our long conflict with the\nMosa and the bloody history we share.
MID_EV13_009_m01_007: I will annex Cybele, the land forever bound to our\nancestors, the Damascar, that it might be ours again.
MID_EV13_009_m01_008: And I will make it a holy land dedicated to worship\nof Yu Phas, restoring her rightful place.
MID_EV13_009_m01_009: Mark me, all of you! I know what honor is!
MID_EV13_009_m01_010: I know the boundless love of our mother goddess,\nYu Phas!
MID_EV13_009_m01_011: And today I promise you that I will repay our debt to\nYu Phas with my body and soul!
MID_EV13_009_m01_012: All hail Queen Theodora!
MID_EV13_009_m01_013: The people love Queen Theodora. Many are hailing\nher as the second coming of the hero Mahadu.
MID_EV13_009_m01_014: Kumos... What I am about to say will sound strange.
MID_EV13_009_m01_015: I would prefer it stay between us.
MID_EV13_009_m01_016: Why all this preamble? It's not like you.
MID_EV13_009_m01_017: Lately I have wondered if we ought to think more\ncritically of hereditary succession.
MID_EV13_009_m01_018: What?! Ah, excuse me... Please continue.
MID_EV13_009_m01_019: Never have I doubted that my lady—Queen\nTheodora, I should say—is worthy of the throne.
MID_EV13_009_m01_020: However, Prince Dyan is her blood relation, and he\nproved to be a monster.
MID_EV13_009_m01_021: That self-aggrandizing hedonist spared no thought\nfor duty, ideals, or faith.
MID_EV13_009_m01_022: To him, soldiers and citizens alike were mere tools to\nexploit. Their devotion to him was simply assumed.
MID_EV13_009_m01_023: If the queen had accepted her fate quietly...\nOh, I shudder to think.
MID_EV13_009_m01_024: A King Dyan would no doubt have spelled doom\nfor Saramis.
MID_EV13_009_m01_025: All came out well in the end, yet I cannot help\nbut brood.
MID_EV13_009_m01_026: If there's a point at the end of this, you're taking a\nwinding road to get there.
MID_EV13_009_m01_027: It is not the bloodline that deserves our loyalty,\nnor should it determine our king.
MID_EV13_009_m01_028: Rather, I feel it ought to be something less tangible.\nBenevolence...authenticity... Qualities of the heart.
MID_EV13_009_m01_029: Call me naïve if you wish, but I am once again glad\nto owe Queen Theodora my fealty.
MID_EV13_009_m01_030: I feel the same, Bonaventure. I hope that eases\nyour mind.
MID_EV13_009_m01_031: Yet I cannot help but think that were Queen\nTheodora ever blessed with a child...
MID_EV13_009_m01_032: surely her offspring would be a sterling monarch.
MID_EV13_009_m01_033: You are a puzzle, to say that in the same breath as\nyou reject hereditary rule.
MID_EV13_009_m01_034: I know it. Some part of me is too invested in the idea\nof royal lineage to let go.
MID_EV13_009_m01_035: My true feelings are complex and not easily grasped,\neven by me. We humans are strange beasts.